  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Electoral Accountability and Transparency (SEAT)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Nigeria):  With FY 2022 Funds this activity will:Support capacity building of Independent National Electoral Commission (INEC) and state independent electoral; Provide technical assistance to further improve the capacity and commitment of INEC and other election management bodies to deliver credible elections through means such as improved accuracy of the voter register;Sustain improvement of new technology (e.g. biometric card readers); improved internal efficiency and knowledge management; andImprove voter education outreach to marginalized populations (women, youth, persons with disabilities, and internally displaced persons).In preparation for local government elections and off-cycle elections that will take place before and immediately after the scheduled general elections this activity will reinforce the capacity of INEC and other election management bodies to conduct free, fair, transparent, and peaceful elections, thus leading to improved public confidence in Nigeria&apos;s democracy and further promote the credibility and sustainability of electoral institutions. Targeted technical assistance will be used to strengthen the capacity of INEC and other election management bodies to help ensure credible electoral processes are critical to strengthening good governance in Nigeria. Strengthening democratic governance is a key priority of the Integrated Country Strategy for Nigeria, the USAID CDCS, and directly supports Goal 4 of the 2022-20226 Joint Strategic Plan..</narrative>
  </description>
